        "original_id": "22e12195-61f5-5f5f-a642-bf3fe375a5d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Donaldson, André Cayatte, Chris Donaldson\n- Roles: film director, producer, writer, filmmaker, lawyer\n- Films: The World's Fastest Indian, Smash Palace, No Way Out, Thirteen Days, Dante's Peak\n- Places: Carcassonne, Paris, United States, Australia, New Zealand\n- Topics: crime, justice, moral responsibility, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- André Cayatte was born on 3 February 1909 in Carcassonne and died on 6 February 1989 in Paris.\n- André Cayatte was a French filmmaker and lawyer known for films about crime, justice, and moral responsibility.\n- Roger Donaldson was born on 15 November 1945 and is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer, and writer.\n- Roger Donaldson directed films including the 1981 relationship drama Smash Palace, No Way Out (1987), Dante's Peak (1997), Thirteen Days (2000), and The World's Fastest Indian (2005).\n- Roger Donaldson made a run of film titles shot in the United States, including No Way Out, Dante's Peak, and Thirteen Days.\n- Chris Donaldson is the son of film director Roger Donaldson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
